BT 72 720 Td 14 TL /F1 12 Tf (4 The Zephyr-7 Adaptation Scheduler) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Adaptation after deployment alternates between collecting real rollouts and) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (fine-tuning the world model and policy. The Zephyr-7 scheduler allocates these) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (phases adaptively: it triggers a new collection phase only when model) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (disagreement on the current replay buffer exceeds a calibrated threshold, and) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (it lengthens fine-tuning phases geometrically as disagreement decays. Compared) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (with a fixed alternating schedule, Zephyr-7 reduces sim-to-real adaptation) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (time by 38% on TerraHound-4, from a median of 14.2 hours to 8.8 hours of) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (onboard compute.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (The scheduler adds two hyperparameters, the disagreement threshold and the) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (growth factor, and no additional models. Ablation with a disagreement-) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (triggered but constant fine-tuning length recovers only half of the saving,) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (indicating that phase lengthening contributes as much as triggering.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (5 Locomotion Results) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (After adaptation, policies retain 96% of their asymptotic simulated reward on) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (flat terrain, 91% on randomized gravel, and 84% on wet low-friction surfaces.) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (Emergency-stop latency after payload shifts of 3 kg remains within 120 ms for) Tj T* /F1 12 Tf (all Zephyr-7 runs, matching the fixed-schedule baseline.) Tj T* ET
